      "writtenOn": "2023-02-02T04:42:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I looks like COMPARATOR follows the pin\u0027s output value, so we should simply always use that bit instead of ACOK (since the INFO2 values in the log show it falling from 1 to 0 when the comparator output is inverted).\n\n```\n*acok \u003d regval \u0026 RAA489000_INFO2_COMPARATOR;\n\nreturn EC_SUCCESS;\n```\n\nI imagine this also means we want to remove the option for AC_PRESENT_CONTROL entirely because this function would work incorrectly in all cases if it\u0027s disabled, but we can investigate that separately.",
      "parentUuid": "a6fc6d7a_856d2016",
      "revId": "420ffc344e6f573065049aa133d308951b911675",
